          "type": "code-smell",
          "priority": "high",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T10:02:13Z",
          "note": "BLOCKING BUG 1 — views/strategy.js renderStrategyDetail save handler (lines ~265-269): Vision fields are serialized as trimmed strings regardless of whether the user cleared them. When a textarea is empty, (document.getElementById('vision-short').value || '').trim() produces ''. This empty string is sent in the PUT payload as: { vision: { short_term: '', mid_term: '', long_term: '' } }. However StrategicVisionSchema (src/schema/repository-registry.ts) validates each horizon as z.string().min(1).nullable() — empty strings are explicitly rejected with a validation error. The file-level comment in api-repos.ts documents this: 'empty strings are rejected'. Result: a user who clears any vision textarea and clicks Save will get a 400 error ('Invalid request body') — the field cannot be cleared through the UI. Fix: convert empty strings to null before sending: short_term: (document.getElementById('vision-short').value || '').trim() || null. Apply the same pattern to mid_term and long_term."
