          "type": "code-smell",
          "priority": "high",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T10:02:13Z",
          "note": "BLOCKING BUG 2 — views/strategy.js renderStrategyDetail save handler (line ~264): The payload always includes folder_names: collectFolderNamesFromDOM(). If the user removes all folder entries, collectFolderNamesFromDOM() returns []. The backend RepoUpdateBodySchema validates folder_names as z.array(z.string().min(1)).min(1).optional() — an empty array is rejected with a 400 validation error (fieldError on folder_names). Result: a user who removes all folder names and clicks Save will get a 400 error and cannot save. This is a behavioral trap because the 'Remove' button works correctly for individual entries, but the final save silently breaks when the last entry is removed. Fix: before constructing the payload, check if collectFolderNamesFromDOM() is empty. Either (a) show a client-side validation error ('At least one folder name is required') before calling the API — consistent with how the Add Repository form validates empty ID — or (b) omit folder_names from the payload entirely when empty so the field is left unchanged (partial update semantics). Option (a) is preferable for clarity."
