    {
      "from_agent": "Reviewer",
      "to_agent": "Developer",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-05T10:02:13Z",
      "notes": [
        "REVIEW FAIL — 2 Blocking Issues require Developer rework before re-entering the pipeline. BLOCKING BUG 1 (high priority): In renderStrategyDetail save handler (views/strategy.js ~line 265-269), empty vision textarea values are sent as '' (empty string) instead of null. StrategicVisionSchema rejects empty strings (z.string().min(1).nullable()), so any user who clears a vision field will receive a 400 error on Save. Fix: replace '' with null for each horizon — e.g., short_term: (document.getElementById('vision-short').value || '').trim() || null. BLOCKING BUG 2 (high priority): Same save handler always sends folder_names: collectFolderNamesFromDOM(). If all folder entries are removed, the array is [] and the backend rejects it (min(1) on folder_names in RepoUpdateBodySchema). Fix: add client-side validation before submit — if collectFolderNamesFromDOM().length === 0, show an error message ('At least one folder name is required') and abort the API call. ADDITIONAL NOTE: The Add Repository form (renderStrategyList) does not validate that folder_names is non-empty either (it sends [] if the folder field is blank), which will produce the same 400 error from POST /api/repos. This should be fixed in the same rework pass. QA should re-verify: (a) saving with a cleared vision textarea succeeds and saves null to storage; (b) the save form shows a clear error when all folder names are removed; (c) the add-repo form shows a clear error when no folder names are entered."
      ]
